// **The pond with a shore** -- the bed Phase 2 of
// `Reports/aquatic-implementation-plan-2026-09-14.md` is measured in, and the
// only one of the three pond beds in which an animal ever meets water.
//
// `the_pond.ron` sinks its water four rows below a stone lip. That is correct
// for the hydraulic question it asks and useless for the locomotion one:
// measured, ants walking east along that bed stop at x=176, the lip, and the
// animal bounding box never enters the pond's footprint. **They never touch
// the water at all.**
//
// Here the waterline is flush with the bed surface at y=160, so a walking ant
// meets it head-on. Measured at 6x with the marker overlay and rain off,
// frames 7,400-8,000: ants walk out of the bank and **stand on the water
// surface**, five or more cells from the shore. That is
// `open-bugs-handoff.md` §R2's locomotion half, which the owner ruled on
// 2026-08-29 (drown, float and swim, all heritable, float limit mechanical --
// recorded as E9) and which is still unbuilt. Phase 2 is the work that
// changes what this bed shows.
//
// **The colony arrives at frame 6,000, not frame 0**, for the reason
// `the_pond_stocked.ron` gives at length: a colony dropped onto seedlings
// collapses regardless and would confound anything measured here.
//
// Note for whoever runs this: `labgif` defaults `rain=steady`, which puts
// water on the bank and into the pond. Pass `rain=off` for any question about
// where the waterline is.
(
    name: "the_pond_shore",
    title: "THE POND",
    question: "A stone-lined basin filled with water -- does the body stay where it was put, stay full, and stay asleep?",
    bed: (
        width: 512,
        height: 320,
        soil_depth: 96,
        ground_y: 160,
        compartments: 1,
        founders: 0,
        species: "herb",
        colonies: 0,
        colony_ants: 52,
        colony_species: "ant",
        predators: 0,
        lamp_spacing: 33,
        seed: 1,
        extra_walls: [],
    ),
    settings: [],
    placements: [
        // The hole, cut through the bed's surface into the soil.
        Clear(x: 176, y: 160, w: 160, h: 36),
        // The shell: two walls and a floor, so the surrounding soil cannot
        // slump in and the water cannot drain down through the bed.
        Fill(material: "stone", x: 176, y: 160, w: 4, h: 36),
        Fill(material: "stone", x: 332, y: 160, w: 4, h: 36),
        Fill(material: "stone", x: 176, y: 192, w: 160, h: 4),
        // The water, inside the shell, with a four-row lip of air above it
        // so a full basin is visibly not an overflowing one.
        Fill(material: "water", x: 180, y: 160, w: 152, h: 32),
        Plant(species: "herb", x: 60),
        Plant(species: "herb", x: 100),
        Plant(species: "herb", x: 400),
        Plant(species: "herb", x: 450),
    ],
    timeline: [
        (at: 6000, every: 0, until: 0, what: Colony(species: "ant", x: 120, count: 52)),
    ],
    horizon: 30000,
)
